5. Remediation plan   

<table>OrderActionAcceptance evidence1Fix D22 pipeline failure propagation (&#x27;pipeline&#x27; or explicit PIPESTATUS).A negative-control run with a failing Python validator makes the workflow fail; a passing run remains green.2Harden replay policy/archive trust before any execution-enabled replay.Tampered policy/hash and modified executable source are rejected before execution; default remains no-exec.3Bound quadratic verifier workload before allocating candidate sets.Huge coefficient bounds fail quickly with a deterministic validation error and bounded memory use.4Pin GitHub Actions to reviewed commit SHA5.All third-party &#x27;uses&#x27; entries resolve to full SHA pins with release comments.5Add sanitized receipt/report export and explicit data-sharing guidance.Tests prove secret-like command arguments are omitted/redacted in sanitized output.6Pin dependencies and create a resolved dependency inventory/SBOM.Clean-environment install uses locked versions; dependency scan output is attached to a commit-specific receipt.7Run full-history secret scanning and inspect large log artifacts.Tool, version, commit range, result, and any remediation/rotation are recorded.</table>  

===== Page 8 =====

6. Coverage limits and audit integrityThis report records a static source review of a public repository snapshot. It does not claim that the repository is vulnerability- free, and it does not replace an execution- based security test.Not performed in this session:- A full 'git clone' or local checkout. The attempted clone failed because this environment could not resolve 'github.com'; the review proceeded using GitHub connector access to the recursive tree and selected source files.- Execution of repository tests, unit tests, fuzzing, dynamic analysis, or proof builds.- Gitlaks/TrueHog scanning over all current blobs and historical commits.- A resolved dependency installation and CVE/advisory scan; there are no fully pinned dependency versions from which to derive a reliable current SBOM.- Inspection of GitHub repository settings for branch protection, rulesets, secret- scanning configuration, Dependabot alerts, Actions secrets, environment protection rules, or collaborator permissions.- Independent verification of current GitHub Actions outcomes for every workflow.Interpretation rules- A confirmed finding is supported by the inspected source behavior described in the report.- A conditional architecture risk requires the stated preconditions; it is not evidence that exploitation has occurred.- No match in targeted code search is not equivalent to a clean full- history secret scan.- Manifest integrity proves only that listed files match expected digests. It does not establish that every relevant file is listed, that the expected digests are trustworthy, or that the code is mathematically correct.- A passing CI job is only as reliable as its command exit handling, pinned inputs, tested commit, and evidence scope.  

