## Final conclusion  

The review found no confirmed hardcoded credential and no confirmed direct code- execution exploit in the inspected paths. It did identify two correctness/security- boundary issues worth prioritizing (D22 pipeline status propagation and replay input trust) plus a verifier resource- exhaustion risk. The next defensible checkpoint is to fix and negatively test those behaviors, then run a full- history secret scan and dependency scan against a locally cloned, commit- pinned snapshot. Until those steps are completed, the appropriate status is STATIC REVIEW WITH OPEN VALIDATION ITEMS, not "clean" or "certified secure."  

Audit scope and results are tied to the repository snapshot identified on the cover. Re- run the audit after material changes to workflow files, replay policy/controller code, dependency declarations, or evidence- processing tools.
